WEBVTT

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.690
Your Japanese has gotten a lot better.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:19.930
No matter how many years pass,
the warmth of summer never changes.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:27.370
So, whenever this season comes around, I remember the summer of my thirteenth year,

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.380
my days as a young boy, when I knew nothing at all.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.070
Even now, it remains unchanged within me.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.770
Welcome!

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:09.990
Come in.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.310
Are you ready to order?

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.980
I'll have some iced coffee.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.490
I learned Arashi-san's secret.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.140
Arashi-san is actually a ghost,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.190
and she has the power to travel back in time.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.240
This secret is mine and hers alone. I can't tell anyone.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.330
Why are you spacing out, Yasaka?

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:35.760
What? It's nothing! Just a secret that belongs to Arashi-san and me alone...

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.220
Huh?

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.340
What's wrong?

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.020
Yasaka's hiding something about you, I think.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.430
Oh, that.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.640
I'm actually a ghost.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.000
And I have the power to go back in time.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.860
What's got you so shocked?

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.490
Arashi-san, it's not a secret?

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.300
Right. No point in hiding it.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.140
N-No way...

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.580
You're a bit too old to be believing that crap.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.110
Get back to work.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.660
The fact that he doesn't believe it at all pisses me off.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.930
Are you interested in unbelievable stories like that?

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.400
Outpouring Memories

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.500
The speeding ticket I got had a massive fine attached.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.480
Now, I won't even be able to eat.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:34.150
Is there any good... Any food left?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.430
There is!

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:39.500
It's not gonna fill me up, but it's better than nothing.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.050
Hot water, hot water...

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.400
The gas is shut off.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.860
Water'll do.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.170
The water's shut off, too.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.170
Water Company

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.940
So's my cell phone.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.430
Oh, well. Guess I'll just eat it by licking!

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.070
Back from break!

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.610
Arashi here, back to work!

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.040
Thank you.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.460
Who the hell is that?

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.410
Master, you look just like Oiwa.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.870
Another ghost!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:35.240
Those students returned. They said they wanted to make a home movie staring a black-haired girl,

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.530
so I figured I might as well help them out.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.760
They were obviously after Arashi-san!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:47.180
What? If I had to, I could be way cuter than she is.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.890
If they just wanted a girl in a wig,
they wouldn't come all the way here, right?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:55.460
That looks good on you. You could make a living off it.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.660
You're very cute, Jun-chan.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.390
Don't tease me!

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:03.560
I'd sure love to be in a movie...

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.440
I'm sure I'd be great.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.990
Moving pictures sure are pretty lately.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.410
"Moving pictures"?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:16.930
In my time, they always contained propaganda for the war.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.670
War?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.040
You didn't watch romance movies or things like that?

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.660
I did.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.420
<i>The Sisters of Gion</i>. <i>The Naniwa Elegy</i>.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.220
I don't get people's wartime tastes...

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.990
You're a weird kid, you know that?

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.400
You're cute, but a bit off...

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.370
But that's also cute in its own way...

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.440
Somehow, saying that pissed me off.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.600
By the way, where's this movie being made?

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.790
The Ookurayama Girls High School, they said.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:03.410
I'm Arashiyama Sayoko, from the Ookurayama Girls High School.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:04.740
That's...

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.350
Three stations away from here.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:11.280
But they say there are ghosts there.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.350
Ghosts?

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:16.570
It's an old, pre-war wooden building, and it's all dark inside.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:22.090
And they say, in the summer, the ghosts of students who died during the war appear.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.730
Really?

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.200
I wouldn't want something weird to show up on the video...

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.900
Why don't you quit? It's really creepy.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:31.810
Don't be silly. That has nothing to do with it.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:35.450
Being called an "actress" suits me.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.340
Being called the "monster" would sure suit you-

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.700
Stupid kid! I'll strangle you!

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:40.970
Oh, whatever...

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.800
You should try to be an actor, too.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.770
No way!

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.180
Aren't you scared of ghosts?

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.390
The only thing that makes a man weak are tears from the woman he loves.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.520
Then why don't we go there now?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.500
To Ookurayama.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.740
This is...

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.680
It really does feel like ghosts live here.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:14.200
Wait, Arashi-san! We can't just go in without asking.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:19.780
What's wrong, Arashi-san?

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:21.780
It's nothing.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:37.080
The place has changed since I was here.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.630
Arashi-san?

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.760
I know! I'll show you something cool.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.230
This is the library?

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.030
I think it was... Right here.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.120
Good. It's still here.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.730
Look at this.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.750
This is... Arashi-san?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.490
Yup, that's me!

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.630
In an old photo like this?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.660
How?

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:13.040
From my perspective, it was just a short time ago that I was having fun in this room.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.930
I told you, I'm a ghost.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:23.680
What, you still doubt her?

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:26.960
Of course I do. There's no such thing as ghosts.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.730
You were so scared of them yesterday.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.320
That's got nothing to do with this.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.370
I can't believe a story like that.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:37.400
I didn't believe it at first, either. But you saw that, right?

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.910
These days, anyone can use CG to make something like that.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.840
So, what are you going to do?

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.750
Ask a specialist.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.120
You want me to tell you how old this photo is?

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:53.390
This is the oldest place in town, so I thought you might be able to figure it out.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.090
Figure it out?

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.090
I'm the one who took this picture.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.190
It was during the war.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:07.390
I went to the girl's school to take some pictures, and this just happened to be one of them.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.230
She was such a pretty girl.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:21.000
She was from a wealthy family. You can feel her elegance in the picture itself, can't you?

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.720
Amazing!

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.790
She really did live sixty years ago!

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.740
You didn't believe her yourself?

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:35.120
I did! But isn't it cool to have physical proof like this?

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.660
I still think saying she's a ghost is too much.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:39.170
Then what is she?

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:43.470
Um... Maybe she uses makeup to look younger?

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.710
How much would a sixty-year-old need to look that young?

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.620
You met the person who took this picture?

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.080
Yes. He still remembers the day he took it.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.230
Amazing!

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.390
What memories!

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:58.400
Isn't that young man so cool?

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.280
He's an old guy now.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.130
I see. I guess he'd be that old...

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.530
Kinda makes you sigh, hearing stuff like that.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:08.900
Are you sad?

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.990
No, that's not it.

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:14.420
Just, you kinda sigh.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:20.810
This is Sogoru. I was right.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:21.840
There's no doubt about it.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.590
Salt, please.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.560
She was here, too...

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.120
Arashi-chan is late.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.420
I hope she didn't change her mind.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.700
Did you really ask her?

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.010
There she is.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.970
Good morning!

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:55.290
The agency really doesn't like me doing this,

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:01.930
so I wasn't sure. But I figured it was OK to work with you guys.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:05.070
No, we weren't after you...

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:08.530
Because I'm sure you guys are really good!

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:12.520
As an actress, I think this is a good step for me.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:17.620
She even got Japanese straightening for her hair. She's really into it.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.450
Are you sure about this?

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:24.040
If she leaves, Arashi-chan may leave, too...

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.370
Fine. I'll rewrite the script. Hold on.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.880
All right, let's get your makeup on.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.360
OK!

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.860
What is this?!

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.470
You're the old maid who yells at the hero-

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.710
Who's an old maid?

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:46.850
So, she does end up as the master...

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.390
Here comes Arashi-san!

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.270
Wow!

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:03.350
So cute!

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.040
She's just the heroine we wanted!

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.480
Does it look good?

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:08.620
It's perfect!

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:11.120
It's OK, I guess...

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.870
Right. Let's start filming!

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:18.170
Are you really joining the army?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:21.030
If you go, your sister will be left behind.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:26.740
But my brother volunteered. And like a man, he left to fight valiantly!

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:30.580
I can't just stay here and do nothing!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:33.570
He went to protect the people he cared about!

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:38.580
So, shouldn't you protect the person who's closest to you?

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:40.600
Um, yeah...

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:41.610
Cut!

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.250
OK!

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:48.860
Wow, Kamigamo. I never thought you'd be an actor.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.090
You're amazing!

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.350
You want to join our circle for real?

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:58.080
No, actually... Um, the agency...

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.850
All right, next! Arashi-chan, ready?

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.280
Ready!

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:04.840
Scene 15. Cut 3.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.890
The girl remembers her fiancé heading to the battlefield.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.850
What's that?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.850
Ready.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.220
We're rolling.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.630
3, 2...

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:13.650
Action!

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:32.250
How long is this shot?

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:33.950
Cut!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.060
What's wrong, Kamigamo?

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.850
Uh, no. It's nothing...

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.420
Good work.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.410
Where's Arashi-chan?

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.410
Did you ask her to come drinking with us?

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.540
She said she had something to do.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:49.750
I'll go.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.260
Of course, you'll be treating me.

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.320
Kamigamo!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.730
Is this where you've been?

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:10.000
We're going home, Jun-kun.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:10.990
Arashi-san.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.510
I believe you.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.030
Jun, you...

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:19.040
I don't know how to put it. My intuition?

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.280
Your acting just now, the way you moved...

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:25.350
That makes more sense to me than anything.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:26.040
Jun.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.050
That wasn't an act.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.360
That was your true self.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:36.270
You were really alive sixty years ago.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.550
They're stopping filming?

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:43.160
No, actually...

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:47.650
There was noise in all of yesterday's film, so they can't use any of it.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.510
Noise?

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.770
They said they couldn't see a thing in the shots with Arashi.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.150
They're saying maybe it was caused by a ghost.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.070
I guess ghosts do exist.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.650
Maybe it's my fault.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.800
You showed up fine in the picture.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.980
That was when I was still alive.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:10.180
Is this person next to you a friend?

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.050
She was a very good friend named Kaya.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.660
She was really pretty and really quiet.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.180
She's not Japanese, is she?

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.750
She's German.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.120
She has such pure white skin.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.680
We used to play all the time.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.560
I wonder what she's doing now.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.520
You don't know?

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:32.470
We got separated in the chaos after the air raids.

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:40.300
I'm sure she's living peacefully somewhere, a cute and wonderful grandmother.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:41.620
I'm sure...

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:45.330
Man, that brings back memories.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:47.190
I want to see her.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.190
Then, let's go meet her!

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:52.430
If we look, I'm sure we can find her.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.790
Even if she's in Germany.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:55.500
I'll help you!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:58.590
Arashi-san?

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:01.610
That's right. I just need to look for her.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.030
S-Sa...

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:05.860
I just need to look for her.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:10.350
Why didn't such a simple thing ever cross my mind?

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:11.510
Arashi-san?

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:15.450
Jeez... People shouldn't be alone.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.190
Thank you.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:21.200
Wel-

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.700
The girl from the photo...

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:33.880
Why?

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.430
It's been a long time, Arashi.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.940
Kaya...

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:43.880
There we go!

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.320
Over here, too!

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:49.050
I guess, if you look, you can find all kinds of things to eat.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:57.440
Salt, pepper, soy sauce, cooking saké, wasabi in a tube, Tabasco, seven spice blend...

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.460
Why?

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:08.290
You're supposed to be a cute, wonderful grandmother, living peacefully somewhere!

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.240
That's my line.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:14.170
Two people from sixty years ago...

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.750
Arashi-san, this is amazing!

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:19.160
But why?!

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.960
Arashi-san!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.750
Well, whatever.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.030
"Whatever"?!

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:29.600
I don't know why it happened to me, myself...

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:33.350
For now, I'll just be happy I got to see her.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.240
Good to see you, Kaya.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.150
That easygoing way of yours never changes.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:45.510
This photo brings back memories. I'm amazed you carried it this long.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:48.090
It's a symbol of our friendship. Of course I did!

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:49.030
Liar.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:54.420
You forgot that you used it as a bookmark for a library book.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:59.930
Has that habit of losing things gotten any better over the last sixty years?

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:03.560
Of course! Everything I'd have lost is already gone, so I'm fine.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.560
That's not "better."

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:09.140
She lost the diary I exchanged with her, too.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.180
That's not true!

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:13.200
It was on my desk!

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.840
Aren't you a little old for that tone of voice?

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:21.550
Is lying and making excuses all you've learned over the past sixty years?

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.790
Sixty years isn't a "little old."

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.150
It's way too old.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.840
You shouldn't talk about a lady's age.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:32.890
I'm sure you never read it, but that diary had important things written in it.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.980
Important things?

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.170
They're too stupid to talk about now.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:38.930
I want to know!

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.210
It's your fault for losing it.

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:44.410
Fine. If it's that important, I'll go get it.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.120
Hajime-chan, help me.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.980
Are you going back in time?

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.760
Arashi, can you...

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:53.350
That's right. We connected.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.480
OK, then let's go.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.670
Ready, Hajime-chan?

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:00.790
All set!

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:25.050
This is...

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:28.590
Ookurayama Girls High, sixty years ago.

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:39.120
I got a letter yesterday, from my sister who was evacuated. Half of it was blacked out.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:42.920
There's no point in censoring what little kids write, though.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:48.610
I hope this war ends soon. Then my brother could come home from the front lines.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.050
Don't let go.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:53.950
If we get lost, we won't be able to get back.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.870
Hey, Arashiyama-san.

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:58.170
If you're dressed like that, they'll get mad at you.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.690
Yeah.

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:01.280
Sakura

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:04.670
There it is. Kaya's exchange diary.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.480
Oh, I see...

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.070
I'll write an answer.

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.410
We're back!

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:19.290
See, it was there.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.820
I didn't lose it.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:23.960
You're as thoughtless as ever.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:26.810
What's wrong, Hajime-chan?

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:30.450
I know why the diary went missing.

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.810
Because she brought it to this era.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.800
So, what was the important thing written in the diary?

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.800
"If something ever happens and we get separated, let's meet at the Ark."
"Gotcha! I was there waiting!"

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.530
You fulfilled your promise.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.420
Yeah!

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:51.920
To Be Continued

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:26.830
How are you, Yayoi?

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:29.530
I'm very good indeed, Kanako.

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:32.110
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:34.580
I read another fascinating book.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:37.620
My, what was it called?

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:41.900
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:44.200
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:46.340
Yes, gladly.

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:50.890
It was a world ruled by despair.

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:57.660
Giants like elephants, clothed in devils' raiments, taint the land with murder and destruction.

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:01.190
Betrayed by the friend he believed in and lost to despair,

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:04.740
our hero vows to use his vast powers for revenge.

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:09.000
The pain of losing the woman he loved carved into his heart,

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:12.560
he uses his sadness to fuel his war to save the people.

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:16.130
His is the Legend of a True Savior...

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:19.070
My, what a grand story!

00:23:19.070 --> 00:23:23.060
This mighty Messiah had a phrase he would always say.

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:24.990
What is it, would you tell me?

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:29.250
<i>You're already de-</i>

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:32.880
When you think of summer...

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:34.120
You think of swimming.

00:23:34.120 --> 00:23:35.740
I'm very good at swimming.

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:36.640
Freestyle?

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:37.950
Or the breaststroke?

00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.530
Shin. Gyo. So.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:41.710
Those are old-fashioned strokes, aren't they?

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:44.950
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:50.240
<i>Get up bright and early next time!</i>

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:50.240
Illustration by Kawachi Izumi
